{"callerless":false,"callers":[{"excerpt":[{"line":870,"text":"const GGR_WEBHOOK_HELP=`Restart GG Requestz after changing its environment. In GG Requestz 1.5+, the webhook fires when a request becomes approved; enable request.auto_approve or approve it manually. A successful delivery now receives HTTP 202. Rejected payloads receive HTTP 422 and are named in both applications' logs.`;"},{"line":871,"text":"const ROMM_FRIEND_HELP=`Your friend does not need to run ROMarr. If they use RomM, ask them for an account and choose Add a RomM server. RomM publishes a hash for every ROM, so browsing and netplay matching work without installing anything on their server. The account gets the access their RomM grants; ROMarr cannot narrow it.`;"},{"line":872,"text":"const NETPLAY_HELP=`Netplay matches each ROM by its SHA1, not by its title. “Super Mario Kart” can refer to four different ROMs; two incorrect matches may desync within seconds and look like lag. ROMarr can match only games whose hashes it knows.`;"},{"line":873,"text":"const NO_HASHES_HELP=`No hashes have been recorded yet, so all netplay offers will show as missing. ROMarr reads each ROM's SHA1 from the library server automatically.`;"},{"line":874,"text":"const GG_ADDRESS_HELP=`Use {url} on the same Docker network. Otherwise use ROMarr's LAN or HTTPS URL, reachable from GG Requestz.`;"},{"line":875,"text":"const ROM_SITE_HELP=`ROM sites use plain HTTP through the Direct HTTP client. Some sites require a form that their own page submits, so those need the Headless Browser client to load the page and submit the form. Sites that require a CAPTCHA or bot-detection challenge are reported as unavailable instead of being bypassed.`;"},{"line":876,"text":"const DOWNLOAD_STATE_LABELS={queued:'Queued',grabbed:'Grabbed',imported:'Imported',"}],"excerptSha256":"8c57bed87fc0f7f7a6cbe07fb01d7587368dcfe249efd458e570c7240ddd796c","fileSha256":"4a3257389dd4c9ba3d2d473ad95511bc9fdf4b914a5b88216f9a4b698e65c40b","gitBlob":"97b1b1806695